<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mutesa II of Buganda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1924">1924</a>–<a href="/years/1969">1969</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Edward Mutesa, King Freddie</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mutesa II was kabaka of Buganda from 1939. The British exiled him from 1953 to 1955 after he opposed plans for East African federation, a crisis that strengthened Ganda loyalty. He became the first president of independent Uganda in 1963, but in 1966 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milton-obote">Milton Obote</a> attacked his palace and he died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mutesa-ii-of-buganda.jpg" alt="Mutesa II of Buganda" width="320" height="449" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir._Edward_Fredrick_Mutesa,_The_President_of_Uganda_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
